Z||000011||MinnGreenGT||12-21-2001||01:39 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTFiero1:<BR><B>notice how the fence isnt damaged. he must have not hit the fence, thats probably where he rolled to a stop. for the owners sake i hope thats just a kit but i doubt it<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>True... I think it may have just stopped at the fenceline by coincidence.  If you look in the background of the 1st & 3rd photos, you'll notice a dirt "birm" behind them.  That could easily (and most likely) be the cause to most of the damage. It would also explain the large amount of dirt over the whole car & the absense of the front end.<P>About the kit thing... it's definitely real. I've never seen an F50 kit that actually looked 100% like the real thing- dimensions are usually too short (length) & too tall (height).<P>I do find some humor in the volume of (what I assume is) coolant all over the front of the car.  A smashed radiator at a high speed would make quite a mess!<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 12-21-2001).]||||reg||1
